  "asr_text": "When I leave a delivery notice and head off, I do feel a little down, but then I go on to the next house. I wish there were fewer redeliveries if possible. And it's true that they're hard on us. Even so, I can't just say that customers should pay for them. I think it makes more sense to cover the cost through the overall fee for delivering packages than to charge each customer who missed a delivery for that redelivery. To do that, I'd also like companies to think about whether free shipping on online orders should stay as it is. If they review shipping fees, I want them to review how the fees are set, too, so that the money actually goes to the people delivering the packages.",
